Story 4.8 wires the Epic-4 sticky SeverityBanner into the existing
`severity-banner-slot` reserved since Story 1.2b. The banner surfaces
UNSAFE incidents to operators + viewers across the app — one summary
banner per page, count + "View all" link to /incidents, critical-tinted
styling, role="alert" + aria-live="polite", 24h window.

Read-only surface (no Acknowledge button): the state machine does NOT
allow UNSAFE → acknowledge (transitions.ts:92 + transitions.spec.ts:127
pin the cell as INVALID). An inline button would always 409 from UNSAFE
— a broken-UX surface. Operators dismiss via the Kanban. See the spec
Design Notes for the full rationale.

Cache-key identity: the banner reuses KANBAN_ACTIVE_QUERY_KEY from
useKanbanBoardSocket (Story 4.3) — the SAME key the Kanban populates
and the SAME key the socket subscriber mutates on every
`incident:state_changed`. Banner auto-reconciles without a new socket
subscription. SEVERITY_BANNER_QUERY_KEY_EXPORT pins identity against
the Kanban key in the test rig.

403 RBAC path: the banner's queryFn throws the SAME
KanbanRbacDeniedError class the Kanban throws — extracted to its own
module to break the circular import that would otherwise arise from
the banner → KanbanBoard hook chain. The tagged-error instanceof
check at KanbanBoard.tsx:225 (RbacDenied render branch) keeps working
across both consumers.

